    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15391" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-lăquĕo</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>,
				ātum, 1, v. a., <i>to extricate from snares</i> or <i>fetters; to disentangle</i>, <i>unfetter</i>
			(post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 30, 1, 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem a vinculo angoris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 8, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">constantiam animi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. adv. Symm. 2, 147</span></i>
			.</div>
